<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan Palach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan Palach was a Czech student who set himself on fire in Wenceslas Square in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> on 16 January 1969 in protest against the public's resignation after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact">Warsaw Pact</a> invasion. He died three days later, and his funeral became a mass demonstration. Commemorations in January 1989, known as Palach Week, were among the protests that preceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velvet-revolution">Velvet Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-palach.jpg" alt="Jan Palach" width="158" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Úřady · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Palach_foto_z_pr%C5%AFkazu.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
